[[File:DarthVader-MtVStormtroopers.png|thumb|right|280px|Lord Vader, a Dark Lord of the Sith who served as supreme commander of the Imperial fleet during the Galactic Civil War.]]
{{Quote|Ridiculous. Tell whoever-it-is we can't obey any orders unless they activate their holo and state their rank."<br />''[Activates hologram to show himself]'' "Lord.|An Imperial officer and Darth Vader|<ref name="Doctor Aphra (2016) 35">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 35|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 35]]</ref>}}
'''Lord''' was a title, often of [[Monarchy|nobility]], that applied to certain individuals having power and authority over others. "[[Lady]]" was a [[Gender|feminine]] equivalent of "lord."

==History==
[[Lord Jedi]] was an ancient honorific applied to members of the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref> The [[Jedi]]-turned-[[mercenary]] [[Baylan Skoll]] was referred to as "Lord Baylan."<ref name="Part Four">{{Ahsoka|Part Four: Fallen Jedi}}</ref>

[[File:Acme-DarkEntrance.png|thumb|left|300px|Lord Vader leads stormtroopers into battle]]
The [[Sith]] styled themselves as [[Sith Lord]]s or [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Dark Lords of the Sith]]. [[Darth Sidious]] and his first two [[Sith apprentice|apprentices]], [[Maul|Darth Maul]] and [[Dooku|Darth Tyranus]], were all addressed to as "Lord".<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref><ref name="Episode II: Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}}</ref> "Lord Vader" was the typical form of address by [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] personnel, including [[Imperial officer]]s and [[stormtrooper]]s, for the [[Emperor's Fist|Emperor's right-hand]], [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].<ref name="Doctor Aphra (2016) 35" /> Vader was also a [[Imperial Military|military]] [[commander]]<ref name="Character Encyclopedia2">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> who was elevated to the new position of [[supreme commander of the Imperial fleet]].<ref name="rafga">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>

[[General]] [[Grievous]], the [[Supreme Martial Commander of the Separatist Droid Armies|Supreme Commander of the Droid Army]],<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> was addressed to as "my lord" by members of the [[Confederacy military]], such as the [[Dark Acolyte]] [[Asajj Ventress]]<ref name="Rookies">{{TCW|Rookies (episode)}}</ref> and [[TV-94]].<ref name="Grievous Intrigue">{{TCW|Grievous Intrigue}}</ref> Another [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[Executive Separatist Council|leader]] who was referred to by the title was [[Poggle the Lesser]],<ref name="terror">{{TCW|Legacy of Terror}}</ref> [[Archduke]] of [[Geonosis]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>

Many Imperial higher-ups and affiliates were referred to as "Lord," as with [[Grand Vizier]] [[Mas Amedda]],<ref name="Lando 1">[[Lando 1|''Lando'' 1]]</ref> [[Tion (Lord)|Tion]], a high-ranking member of the [[Imperial Navy]].<ref name="TRB">''[[The Rebellion Begins]]''</ref> [[Janu]] was a lord<ref name="Getty">{{Getty|url=thewaltdisneystudios/allaccess/#!asset/hc968sf4xx57p8snxm8pb93s|text=THND-013615 R|author=[[The Walt Disney Company|The Walt Disney Studios]]|date=2026-03-24}}</ref> who also served as a [[commander]] in the unified [[Imperial Remnants]].<ref name="Chapter23">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 23: The Spies}}</ref> "My lord" was also used by the [[Great Mothers]] to address their ally, [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]].<ref name="Part Eight">{{Ahsoka|Part Eight: The Jedi, the Witch, and the Warlord}}</ref>

It was also a term of deference for [[count]]s,<ref name="AND">[[A New Dawn (novel)|''A New Dawn'']]</ref><ref name="CA">{{TCW|Counterattack}}</ref>

